--TEST--
Every `@tag` in a doc comment outside `@see`, `@example`, `@param`, `@return` and `@throws` is `E0128` — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/doc-comments
// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`: the set is closed, so
// every other `@tag` is a diagnostic. A retired PHPDoc name and an invented
// name get the same error.
/// Charges a card, in the smallest unit the currency has.
///
/// @since 1.2
/// @ledger nothing reads this
final class Till {
    public static function charge(int $cents): int {
        return $cents;
    }
}
echo Till::charge(1), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0128]: `@since` is not a documentation tag
  --> %s:8:5
  |
8 | /// @since 1.2
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^ not one of the five tags
  = help: a doc comment is Markdown. The only tags are `@see`, `@example`, `@param`, `@return` and `@throws`

error[E0128]: `@ledger` is not a documentation tag
  --> %s:9:5
  |
9 | /// @ledger nothing reads this
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not one of the five tags
  = help: a doc comment is Markdown. The only tags are `@see`, `@example`, `@param`, `@return` and `@throws`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
